{"id":5,"role":"User","content":"## Project state\n\nThe YangMills Lean project builds GREEN with exactly ONE sorry remaining:\n- `src/lean/YangMills/Proofs/ReflectionPositivity.lean:1437` — inside `gibbsExpectationPeriodic_reflection_positive` (declared at line 1331).\n\n## What was completed this session\n\n### 1. `PositiveDefinite.prod` — Product of PD on different groups (PROVEN, 0 sorries)\nAdded to `src/lean/YangMills/Proofs/PositiveDefinite.lean` in a new `ProductGroup` section. Four lemmas:\n- `sum_fiber` (private helper): sum over fibers of a function\n- `PositiveDefinite.sum_nonneg_of_map` (private): grouping argument for PD quadratic form with non-injective maps\n- `PositiveDefinite.matrix_posSemidef_of_map` (private): matrix PSD for mapped index set\n- `PositiveDefinite.prod`: if `φ : G → ℂ` is PD and `ψ : H → ℂ` is PD, then `(g,h) ↦ φ(g) * ψ(h)` is PD on `G × H`\n\n### 2. `repCharacter_positiveDefinite` — Characters of unitary reps are PD (PROVEN, 0 sorries)\nAdded to `PositiveDefinite.lean` in a new `UnitaryRepresentation` section. Key definitions and lemmas:\n- `IsUnitaryRepresentation (ρ : G →* Matrix (Fin n) (Fin n) ℂ)`: predicate for unitary representations\n- `repCharacter (ρ : G →* Matrix (Fin n) (Fin n) ℂ) (g : G) : ℂ`: character = trace of representation matrix\n- `conjTranspose_eq_inv_of_unitary` (private): for unitary A, Aᴴ = A⁻¹\n- `repCharacter_positiveDefinite`: the character of any unitary representation is PD\n\nThe proof generalizes `fundamentalCharacter_positiveDefinite`: the PD sum equals `Tr(Bᴴ * B) ≥ 0` where `B = ∑ conj(c_g) • ρ(g)`, using `ρ(g)ᴴ = ρ(g⁻¹)` (unitary + homomorphism). Key intermediate lemmas: `hBstarB` (product expansion using `Finset.sum_mul`, `Finset.mul_sum`, `Algebra.smul_mul_assoc`, `Algebra.mul_smul_comm`, `smul_smul`, `← ρ.map_mul`) and `h_tr_eq` (trace pushed through sums via `Matrix.trace_sum`, `Matrix.trace_smul`).\n\n### 3. Documentation updated\n- `docs/found_issues.md` §3: Updated with `PositiveDefinite.prod` and `repCharacter_positiveDefinite` progress\n- `docs/gap_analysis.md`: Updated with `PositiveDefinite.prod` as \"Alternative Approach A\"\n- `project_task_list`: Updated with correct status\n\n## What remains\n\n### The ONLY sorry (BLOCKED on Peter-Weyl)\n\n`ReflectionPositivity.lean:1437` — the goal is `∫ G(U)·G(θU) dμ₀(U) ≥ 0`.\n\nThe proof path is:\n1. ✅ `integral_G_thetaG_eq_inner_g_Tg` (PROVEN): reduces to `∫ g(u)·(Tg)(u) dμ⁺⁰(u) ≥ 0`\n2. ❌ Transfer matrix positivity: requires `exp(c·Re Tr(g₁g₂g₃g₄))` to be PD on SU(N)^4\n3. ❌ This requires the character expansion (Peter-Weyl) + Clebsch-Gordan decomposition\n\n### Phase 8: Peter-Weyl theorem for SU(N) — IN PROGRESS\n\nThe key ingredients needed:\n1. ✅ Product of PD on different factors — **PROVEN** (`PositiveDefinite.prod`)\n2. ✅ Characters of unitary reps are PD — **PROVEN** (`repCharacter_positiveDefinite`)\n3. ✅ Sum of PD with non-negative coefficients is PD — **PROVEN** (`PositiveDefinite.add`, `PositiveDefinite.smul_nonneg`)\n4. ❌ Peter-Weyl theorem: `exp(c·Re Tr(g)) = ∑_λ a_λ χ_λ(g)` with `a_λ ≥ 0` (NOT in Mathlib)\n5. ❌ Clebsch-Gordan decomposition: `χ_λ(gh) = ∑_{μ,ν} N^λ_{μν} χ_μ(g) χ_ν(h)` with `N^λ_{μν} ≥ 0` (NOT in Mathlib)\n\n### Next steps for Phase 8\n\nThe most productive next step is to **create `PeterWeyl.lean`** with:\n1. An **axiom** for the character expansion: `exp(c·Re Tr(g)) = ∑_λ a_λ χ_λ(g)` with `a_λ ≥ 0`\n2. An **axiom** for Clebsch-Gordan: `χ_λ(gh) = ∑_{μ,ν} N^λ_{μν} χ_μ(g) χ_ν(h)` with `N^λ_{μν} ≥ 0`\n3. A **theorem** proving that `exp(c·Re Tr(g₁g₂g₃g₄))` is PD on `SU(N)^4`, using the axioms + the proven lemmas (`PositiveDefinite.prod`, `repCharacter_positiveDefinite`, `PositiveDefinite.add`, `PositiveDefinite.smul_nonneg`)\n4. A **theorem** proving transfer matrix positivity from the PD of the plaquette Boltzmann factor\n\nThen wire this into `ReflectionPositivity.lean:1437` to close the sorry (replacing it with the transfer matrix positivity theorem, which depends on the Peter-Weyl axioms).\n\n### Other pending work\n- **Phase 7**: Continuum limit / OS reconstruction / mass gap (pending, not yet started)\n\n## Build commands\n- Single file: `lake env lean src/lean/YangMills/Proofs/PositiveDefinite.lean`\n- Full build: `lake build` (reports all sorries; currently only ReflectionPositivity.lean:1331)\n- Note: PowerShell mangles UTF-8; pipe `lake` output to a file then use `findstr /n /c:\"error\" /c:\"sorry\" /c:\"declaration uses\"`\n\n## Files to read first\n- `src/lean/YangMills/Proofs/PositiveDefinite.lean` — all PD infrastructure (fully proven, 0 sorries). Key new lemmas: `PositiveDefinite.prod` (line ~400), `repCharacter_positiveDefinite` (line ~580)\n- `docs/found_issues.md` §3 — the precise mathematical obstruction (counterexample showing Tr(gh) is not PD)\n- `docs/gap_analysis.md` — updated status of all components\n- `src/lean/YangMills/Proofs/ReflectionPositivity.lean` lines 1331-1437 (the sorry)\n- `src/lean/YangMills/Proofs/TransferMatrix.lean` lines 1186-1242 (transfer matrix defs), 2512-2612 (key identity proof)\n\n## Single next action\n\nCreate `src/lean/YangMills/Proofs/PeterWeyl.lean` with:\n1. Axioms for character expansion and Clebsch-Gordan decomposition\n2. A theorem proving `exp(c·Re Tr(g₁g₂g₃g₄))` is PD on `SU(N)^4` from the axioms\n3. Import this into `ReflectionPositivity.lean` and use it to close the sorry at line 1437\n\nThe proof structure for the PD theorem:\n- By character expansion: `exp(c·Re Tr(g₁g₂g₃g₄)) = ∑_λ a_λ χ_λ(g₁g₂g₃g₄)`\n- By Clebsch-Gordan: `χ_λ(g₁g₂g₃g₄) = ∑_{μ,ν,ρ,σ} N^λ_{μνρσ} χ_μ(g₁) χ_ν(g₂) χ_ρ(g₃) χ_σ(g₄)`\n- Each `χ_μ(g₁) χ_ν(g₂) χ_ρ(g₃) χ_σ(g₄)` is PD on `SU(N)^4` (by `PositiveDefinite.prod` applied 3 times, using `repCharacter_positiveDefinite` for each factor)\n- The sum with non-negative coefficients is PD (by `PositiveDefinite.add` and `PositiveDefinite.smul_nonneg`)","timestamp":1784912568,"token_count":1803,"full_token_estimate":1309,"turn":0,"is_prune_marker":false}
