{"id":7,"role":"Tool","content":"C:\\github\\YangMills\\src\\lean\\YangMills\\Proofs\\PositiveDefinite.lean\n-- 641 lines, 30782 bytes --\n  1 | /-\n  2 | # Positive-Definite Functions on Groups\n  3 | \n  4 | A function φ : G → ℂ on a group G is called *positive-definite* if for any\n  5 | finite set {g₁, ..., gₙ} ⊂ G and coefficients {c₁, ..., cₙ} ⊂ ℂ:\n  6 | \n  7 |     Σ_{i,j} c_i · conj(c_j) · φ(g_i⁻¹ g_j) ≥ 0\n  8 | \n  9 | ## References\n 10 | \n 11 | * K. Osterwalder, E. Seiler, \"Gauge Field Theories on a Lattice\"\n 12 |   (Ann. Phys. 110, 1978, pp 440–471), §3.\n 13 | -/\n 14 | \n 15 | import Mathlib.Analysis.Complex.Basic\n 16 | import Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.Trace\n 17 | import Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.UnitaryGroup\n 18 | import Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Exp\n 19 | import Mathlib.Analysis.Matrix.Order\n 20 | import Mathlib.Analysis.Normed.Algebra.Exponential\n 21 | import Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Exponential\n 22 | import Mathlib.Topology.Algebra.Monoid\n 23 | import Mathlib.Topology.Order.OrderClosed\n 24 | import Mathlib.Topology.Algebra.InfiniteSum.NatInt\n 25 | import YangMills.SpecialUnitary\n 26 | open Finset\n 27 | open Complex\n 28 | open Filter\n 29 | open Matrix\n 30 | open scoped ComplexConjugate\n 31 | open scoped ComplexOrder\n 32 | \n 33 | namespace YangMills\n 34 | \n 35 | /-- A function φ : G → ℂ is positive-definite. -/\n 36 | def PositiveDefinite {G : Type*} [Group G] (φ : G → ℂ) : Prop :=\n 37 |   ∀ (s : Finset G) (c : G → ℂ),\n 38 |     (∑ i ∈ s, ∑ j ∈ s, c i * conj (c j) * φ (i⁻¹ * j)) ≥ 0\n 39 | \n 40 | section BasicProperties\n 41 | \n 42 | variable {G : Type*} [Group G] {φ ψ : G → ℂ}\n 43 | \n 44 | lemma PositiveDefinite.add (hφ : PositiveDefinite φ) (hψ : PositiveDefinite ψ) :\n 45 |     PositiveDefinite (λ g => φ g + ψ g) := by\n 46 |   intro s c\n 47 |   have h1 := hφ s c\n 48 |   have h2 := hψ s c\n 49 |   have hsum : (∑ i ∈ s, ∑ j ∈ s, c i * conj (c j) * ((λ g => φ g + ψ g) (i⁻¹ * j))) =\n 50 |       (∑ i 