{"id":19,"role":"Tool","content":"C:\\github\\YangMills\\src\\lean\\YangMills\\Proofs\\ReflectionPositivity.lean\n-- 1497 lines, 93153 bytes --\n 1 | /-\n 2 | # Reflection Positivity on the Lattice\n 3 | \n 4 | Reflection positivity (Osterwalder-Schrader positivity) is the key axiom\n 5 | connecting Euclidean quantum field theory to Minkowski quantum field theory\n 6 | via the OS reconstruction theorem.\n 7 | \n 8 | For SU(N) lattice gauge theory, reflection positivity states:\n 9 | \n10 |     ⟨f θ(f)⟩ ≥ 0\n11 | \n12 | for any observable f depending only on link variables in the positive-time\n13 | half-lattice (t > 0). Here θ is the time-reflection map:\n14 | \n15 |     (θ U)(n, μ) = U(θ n, μ)⁻¹   if μ = 0 (time direction)\n16 |     (θ U)(n, μ) = U(θ n, μ)     if μ ≠ 0 (spatial direction)\n17 | -/\n18 | \n19 | import YangMills.Lattice\n20 | import YangMills.SpecialUnitary\n21 | import YangMills.Proofs.LatticeMeasure\n22 | import YangMills.Proofs.BasicLemmas\n23 | import Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.Trace\n24 | \n25 | set_option linter.unusedVariables false\n26 | set_option maxHeartbeats 2000000\n27 | namespace YangMills\n28 | namespace Lattice\n29 | \n30 | /--\n31 | The reflection of an observable on any lattice type with `ReflectSite`:\n32 |     (θ f)(U) = f(θ U)\n33 | where θ acts on link variables via `reflectLinkVariable`.\n34 | -/\n35 | def reflectObservable (N : ℕ) {Λ : Type} [ReflectSite Λ] (f : LinkVariable (SU N) Λ → ℝ) :\n36 |     LinkVariable (SU N) Λ → ℝ :=\n37 |   λ U => f (reflectLinkVariable N U)\n38 | \n39 | lemma reflectObservable_involution (N : ℕ) {Λ : Type} [ReflectSite Λ] (f : LinkVariable (SU N) Λ → ℝ)\n40 |     (U : LinkVariable (SU N) Λ) : reflectObservable N (reflectObservable N f) U = f U := by\n\n... 1457 more line(s) below (use offset=41 to continue reading)","timestamp":1784912970,"token_count":545,"tool_call_id":"e21c73d6-f0df-4c39-b86e-a1c55dbe9a64","full_token_estimate":418,"tool_meta":{"tool_name":"read_file","file_path":"src/lean/Y