{"id":42,"role":"Tool","content":"Search results (5):\n\n1. [https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/BF01614090]\n   Construction of a selfadjoint, strictly positive transfer matrix for ...\n   It is shown that physical positivity holds in Wilson's lattice gauge theories, i.e. transition probabilities between gauge invariant states are non-negative and the quantum mechanical Hamiltonian has real eigenvalues only.\n\n2. [https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/Definition-and-General-Properties-of-the-Transfer-L%C3%BCscher-Weisz/8eb816929a834c124b66316914c50eedaf69b423]\n   Definition and General Properties of the Transfer Matrix in Continuum ...\n   When operators of dimension 6 are added to the standard Wilson action in lattice gauge theories, physical positivity is lost in general. We show that a transfer matrix can nevertheless be defined. Its properties are, however, unusual: complex eigenvalues may occur (leading to damped oscillatory behaviour of correlation functions), and there are always contributions in the spectral ...\n\n3. [https://projecteuclid.org/journals/communications-in-mathematical-physics/volume-54/issue-3/Construction-of-a-selfadjoint-strictly-positive-transfermatrix-for-euclidean-lattice/cmp/1103900872.full]\n   Construction of a selfadjoint, strictly positive transfer matrix for ...\n   1977 Construction of a selfadjoint, strictly positive transfer matrix for euclidean lattice gauge theories M. Lüscher\n\n4. [https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/0550321384902700]\n   Definition and general properties of the transfer matrix in continuum ...\n   When operators of dimension 6 are added to the standard Wilson action in lattice gauge theories, physical positivity is lost in general. We show that a transfer matrix can nevertheless be defined. Its properties are, however, unusual: complex eigenvalues may occur (leading to damped oscillatory behaviour of correlation functions), and there are always contributions in the spectral ...\n\n5. [https://www.osti.gov/etdeweb/biblio/6087876]\n   Definition and general properties of the transfer matrix in continuum ...\n   When operators of dimension 6 are added to the standard Wilson action in lattice gauge theories, physical positivity is lost in general. We show that a transfer matrix can nevertheless be defined.\n\n","timestamp":1784915464,"token_count":572,"tool_call_id":"73cbc8ab-0565-45c4-a289-08486a5627e0","full_token_estimate":532,"tool_meta":{"tool_name":"web_search","file_path":null,"old_text":"Lüscher \"transfer matrix\" lattice gauge theory reflection positivity proof character expansion positive operator","new_text":null,"exit_code":null,"line_count":null,"byte_count":2277,"is_error":false,"duration_ms":1400,"edit_line":null},"turn":24,"is_prune_marker":false}
{"id":43,"role":"Tool","content":"Search results (5):\n\n1. [https://ui.adsabs.harvard.edu/abs/1978AnPhy.110..440O/abstract]\n   Gauge field theories on a lattice - NASA/ADS\n   We begin a rigorous, nonperturbative investigation of quantum field theories with local internal symmetries. We discuss the lattice approximation of Yang-Mills fields and of fermion fields in the Euclidean setup and we verify physical positivity for the Schwinger functions of these approximations. This implies the existence of a positive self-adjoint transfer matrix. We then prove existence ...\n\n2. [https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/0003491678900398]\n   Gauge field theories on a lattice - ScienceDirect\n   This implies the existence of a positive self-adjoint transfer matrix. We then prove existence and analyticity of the infinite volume limit of strongly coupled Yang-Mills theories on the lattice and we verify Wilson's confinement bound. Finally we present a rigorous treatment of the Higgs mechanism in lattice gauge theories.\n\n3. [https://inspirehep.net/literature/251466]\n   Osterwalder-schrader Positivity for the Wilson Action\n   Osterwalder-Seiler's proof of reflection positivity of lattice gauge theories with fermions is extended to the case in which the reflection is performed with respect to planes containing sites. Our proof applies to all observables and relies on the particular structure of the Wiklson action.\n\n4. [https://archive.org/download/wikipedia-scholarly-sources-corpus/10.1016%252F0001-4575%252871%252990016-9.zip/10.1016%252F0003-4916%252878%252990039-8.pdf]\n   PDF PII: 0003-4916(78)90039-8 - Archive.org\n   We begin a rigorous, nonperturbative investigation of quantum field theories with local internal symmetries. We discuss the lattice approximation of Yang-Mills fields and offer- mion fields in the Euclidean setup and we verify physical positivity for the Schwinger functions of these approximations. This implies the existence of a positive self-adjoint transfer matrix. We then prove existence ...\n\n5. [https://projecteuclid.org/journals/communications-in-mathematical-physics/volume-113/issue-3/General-proof-of-Osterwalder-Schrader-positivity-for-the-Wilson-action/cmp/1104160284.pdf]\n   PDF General Proof of Osterwalder-Schrader Positivity for the Wilson Action\n   Abstract We extend the proof by Osterwalder and Seiler of reflection positivity of lattice gauge theories with fermions to the case in which the reflection is performed with respect to planes containing sites. Our proof applies to all observables and relies on the particular structure of the Wilson action. This assures the positivity of the correlation functions\n\n","timestamp":1784915464,"token_count":663,"tool_call_id":"d6281068-5bba-47c9-a787-39d7a7d92667","full_token_estimate":613,"tool_meta":{"tool_name":"web_search","file_path":null,"old_text":"Osterwalder Seiler 1978 reflection positivity lattice gauge theory plaquette character expansion proof","new_text":null,"exit_code":null,"line_count":null,"byte_count":2639,"is_error":false,"duration_ms":1198,"edit_line":null},"turn":24,"is_prune_marker":false}
