{"id":50,"role":"Tool","content":"C:\\github\\YangMills\\src\\lean\\YangMills\\Proofs\\ReflectionPositivity.lean\n-- 1497 lines, 93153 bytes --\n1440 | structure PeriodicExpectation (N T L : ℕ) (β : ℝ) [NeZero T] [NeZero L] (hT : Odd T) : Type 1 where\n1441 |   /-- The partition function Z = ∫ exp(-S_W) dU. -/\n1442 |   partitionFunction : ℝ\n1443 |   /-- Positivity of the partition function: Z > 0 for β > 0. -/\n1444 |   partitionFunctionPos : partitionFunction > 0\n1445 |   /-- The expectation of an observable F. -/\n1446 |   evaluate : (LinkVariable (SU N) (PeriodicSite T L) → ℝ) → ℝ\n1447 |   /-- Linearity of expectation. -/\n1448 |   linearity : ∀ (a b : ℝ) (F G : LinkVariable (SU N) (PeriodicSite T L) → ℝ),\n1449 |     (MeasureTheory.Integrable (λ (cfg : FiniteLinkConfig N (PeriodicSite T L) (Finset.univ : Finset (PeriodicSite T L))) =>\n1450 |       F (extendLinkVariable N (PeriodicSite T L) (Finset.univ : Finset (PeriodicSite T L)) cfg) *\n1451 |       Real.exp (-β * wilsonActionFiniteConfig N β (PeriodicSite T L) (Finset.univ : Finset (PeriodicSite T L)) cfg))\n1452 |       (productHaarMeasure N (PeriodicSite T L) (Finset.univ : Finset (PeriodicSite T L)))) →\n1453 |     (MeasureTheory.Integrable (λ (cfg : FiniteLinkConfig N (PeriodicSite T L) (Finset.univ : Finset (PeriodicSite T L))) =>\n1454 |       G (extendLinkVariable N (PeriodicSite T L) (Finset.univ : Finset (PeriodicSite T L)) cfg) *\n1455 |       Real.exp (-β * wilsonActionFiniteConfig N β (PeriodicSite T L) (Finset.univ : Finset (PeriodicSite T L)) cfg))\n1456 |       (productHaarMeasure N (PeriodicSite T L) (Finset.univ : Finset (PeriodicSite T L)))) →\n1457 |     evaluate (λ U => a * F U + b * G U) = a * evaluate F + b * evaluate G\n1458 |   /-- Normalization: ⟨1⟩ = 1. -/\n1459 |   normalization : evaluate (λ _ => 1) = 1\n1460 |   /-- Positivity: if F ≥ 0 pointwise, then evaluate F ≥ 0. -/\n1461 |   positivity : ∀ (F : LinkVariable (SU N) (PeriodicSite T L) → ℝ),\n1462 |     (∀ U, F U ≥ 0) → evaluate F ≥ 0\n1463 |   /-- Reflection positivity: if f depends only on positive+interface links, then ⟨f · θ(f)⟩ ≥ 0. -/\n1464 |   reflectionPositive : ∀ (f : LinkVariable (SU N) (PeriodicSite T L) → ℝ),\n1465 |     dependsOnlyOnPosInterface N T L f →\n1466 |     evaluate (λ U => f U * reflectObservable N f U) ≥ 0\n1467 | /--\n1468 | Construct a `PeriodicExpectation` for the Wilson action on a finite periodic lattice.\n1469 | This uses the Osterwalder-Seiler factorization to prove reflection positivity without\n1470 | the `hadd` limitation of the Z4Site version.\n1471 | -/\n1472 | noncomputable def wilsonPeriodicExpectation (N T L : ℕ) (β : ℝ) [NeZero T] [NeZero L] (hT : Odd T) :\n1473 |     PeriodicExpectation N T L β hT :=\n1474 |   {\n1475 |     partitionFunction := partitionFunctionFinite N β (PeriodicSite T L) (Finset.univ : Finset (PeriodicSite T L))\n1476 |     partitionFunctionPos := partitionFunctionFinite_pos N β (PeriodicSite T L) (Finset.univ : Finset (PeriodicSite T L))\n1477 |     evaluate := gibbsExpectation N β (PeriodicSite T L) (Finset.univ : Finset (PeriodicSite T L))\n1478 |     linearity := λ a b F G hF hG =>\n1479 |       gibbsExpectation_linear N β (PeriodicSite T L) (Finset.univ : Finset (PeriodicSite T L)) a b F G hF hG\n1480 |     normalization := gibbsExpectation_normalization N β (PeriodicSite T L) (Finset.univ : Finset (PeriodicSite T L))\n1481 |     positivity := λ F hF => gibbsExpectation_pos N β (PeriodicSite T L) (Finset.univ : Finset (PeriodicSite T L)) F hF\n1482 |     reflectionPositive := λ f hf_supported =>\n1483 |       gibbsExpectationPeriodic_reflection_positive N T L β hT f hf_supported\n1484 |   }\n1485 | /--\n1486 | The SU(N) lattice Yang-Mills measure with the Wilson action on a finite periodic lattice\n1487 | is reflection positive for observables that depend only on links in the positive-time\n1488 | and interface (time-0) regions.  This is the content of the Osterwalder-Seiler theorem.\n1489 | -/\n1490 | theorem lattic