{"id":57,"role":"Tool","content":"C:\\github\\YangMills\\src\\lean\\YangMills\\Proofs\\TransferMatrix.lean\n-- 2612 lines, 88303 bytes --\n  1 | /-\n  2 | \n  3 | # Transfer Matrix: Corrected Approach\n  4 | \n  5 | \n  6 | \n  7 | This file provides definitions and lemmas toward a transfer matrix proof\n  8 | \n  9 | of the Osterwalder-Seiler reflection positivity for the periodic lattice.\n 10 | \n 11 | \n 12 | \n 13 | ## Mathematical Setup\n 14 | \n 15 | \n 16 | \n 17 | Let μ₀ = μ⁺ ⊗ μ⁻ ⊗ μ⁰ be the factorization of the product Haar measure on\n 18 | \n 19 | the finite periodic lattice into positive-time, negative-time, and interface\n 20 | \n 21 | links (via `measure_factorization'`).\n 22 | \n 23 | \n 24 | \n 25 | For an observable f depending only on links in the positive-time and interface\n 26 | \n 27 | regions (`dependsOnlyOnPosInterface N T L f`), define:\n 28 | \n 29 | \n 30 | \n 31 |     G(U) = f(U)·exp(-β·S_OS⁺(U))·exp(-β·S_OS_int(U)/2)\n 32 | \n 33 |     g(u) = f(u)·exp(-β·S_OS⁺(u)/2)   for u ∈ PosInterfaceConfig\n 34 | \n 35 | \n 36 | \n 37 | The reflection positivity lemma `gibbsExpectationPeriodic_reflection_positive`\n 38 | \n 39 | reduces to proving:\n 40 | \n 41 | \n 42 | \n 43 |     ∫ G(U)·G(θU) dμ₀(U) ≥ 0\n 44 | \n 45 | \n 46 | \n 47 | ## The Correct Transfer Matrix\n 48 | \n 49 | \n 50 | \n 51 | Define the transfer matrix T acting on functions ψ : PosInterfaceConfig → ℝ by:\n 52 | \n 53 | \n 54 | \n 55 |     (T ψ)(U⁺,U⁰) = ∫ ψ(θ⁻⁰(U⁻,U⁰))\n 56 | \n 57 |                      · exp(-β·(S_OS⁻(U⁻)+S_OS_int(U⁺,U⁻,U⁰))/2)\n 58 | \n 59 |                      dμ⁻(U⁻)\n 60 | \n 61 | \n 62 | \n 63 | where θ⁻⁰(U⁻,U⁰) is the restriction of θ(merge(U⁻,U⁰)) to positive+interface\n 64 | \n 65 | sites (i.e., reflecting the negative links to the positive side).\n 66 | \n 67 | \n 68 | \n 69 | ## Key Identity\n 70 | \n 71 | \n 72 | \n 73 |     ∫ G(U)·G(θU) dμ₀(U) = ∫_{PosInt} g(u)·(T g)(u) dμ⁺⁰(u)\n 74 | \n 75 | \n 76 | \n 77 | This holds because:\n 78 | \n 79 | 1. G(U)·G(θU) = g(U⁺,U⁰)·g(θ⁻⁰(U⁻,U⁰))\n 80 | \n 81 |                 · exp(-β·(S_OS⁻(U⁻)+S_OS_int(U⁺,U⁻,U⁰))/2)\n 82 | \n 83 | 2. The factorization μ₀ ≅ μ⁺ × μ⁻ × μ⁰ turns the LHS into an integral\n 84 | \n 85 |    over U⁺,U⁻,U⁰ of this expression.\n 86 | \n 87 | 3. Integrating out U⁻ gives (T g)(U⁺,U⁰) by definition.\n 88 | \n 89 | \n 90 | \n 91 | ## Positivity\n 92 | \n 93 | \n 94 | \n 95 | The operator T is POSITIVE because its integral kernel is a positive-definite\n 96 | \n 97 | function on (SU(N)ⁿ × SU(N)ⁿ). This follows from the Peter-Weyl theorem on\n 98 | \n 99 | SU(N) (Osterwalder-Seiler 1979, Theorem 3.1). Therefore ⟨g, T·g⟩ ≥ 0.\n100 | \n101 | \n102 | \n103 | ## Previous (Incorrect) Approach\n104 | \n105 | \n106 | \n107 | A previous version of this file defined a different transfer matrix that acted\n108 | \n109 | trivially (as a multiplication operator) because it did not apply the reflection\n110 | \n111 | θ⁻⁰ in the kernel.  This made the identity `transferMatrix_identity` false for\n112 | \n113 | general f.  The current approach corrects this by applying the reflection.\n114 | \n115 | \n116 | \n117 | ## References\n118 | \n119 | \n120 | \n121 | - K. Osterwalder, E. Seiler, \"Gauge Field Theories on a Lattice\"\n122 | \n123 |   (Ann. Phys. 110, 1978, pp 440–471), §3.\n124 | \n125 | - J. Glimm, A. Jaffe, \"Quantum Physics\" (2nd ed.), §6.1.\n126 | \n127 | - M. Lüscher, \"Some analytic results concerning the mass spectrum\n128 | \n129 |   of Yang-Mills gauge theories on a torus\" (1983)\n130 | \n131 | - M. Salmhofer, \"Construction of a Higgs field\" (thesis, 1990).\n132 | \n133 | -/\n134 | \n135 | \n136 | \n137 | import YangMills.Proofs.ReflectionPositivity\n138 | \n139 | import Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Measure.MeasureSpaceDef\n140 | \n141 | import Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Constructions.Pi\n142 | \n143 | import Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Exp\n144 | \n145 | import Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Measure.Haar.Basic\n146 | \n147 | import Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.Prod\n148 | \n149 | \n150 | \n151 | open Set\n152 | \n153 | open Matrix\n154 | \n155 | open scoped BigOperators\n156 | \n157 | open MeasureTheory\n158 | \n159 | \n160 | \n161 | namespace YangMills\n162 | \n163 | namespace Lattice\n164 | \n165 | \n166 | \n167 | section TransferMatrix\n168 | \n169 | \n170 | \n\n... 2442 more line(s) below (use offset=171 to continue reading)","timestamp":1784917042,"token_count":1303,"tool_call_id":"4baf6e4c-f2ed-46d4-92e4-1ce3c0adc4c7","full_token_estimate":988,"tool_meta":{"tool_name":"read_file","file_path":"src/lean/YangMills/Proofs/TransferMatrix.lean","old_text":null,"new_text":null,"exit_code":null,"line_count":2612,"byte_count":88303,"is_error":false,"duration_ms":0,"edit_line":null},"turn":33,"is_prune_marker":false}
